1
00:00:45,253 --> 00:00:48,965
PERFECT CROWN

2
00:00:54,216 --> 00:00:55,631
SPONSORED BY: MINISTRY OF
CULTURE, SPORTS AND TOURISM

3
00:00:55,712 --> 00:00:57,213
AND KOREA CREATIVE
CONTENT AGENCY

4
00:00:57,536 --> 00:00:59,473
MBC DRAMA SCRIPT
CONTEST WINNER

5
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:00,977
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION

6
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,979
CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
WERE FILMED SAFELY

7
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:14,574
Your Royal Highness, is your
scandal with CEO Seong Huiju true?

8
00:01:14,657 --> 00:01:16,576
Why was a doctor called to the hotel?

9
00:01:16,659 --> 00:01:17,911
Would you care to respond?

10
00:01:17,994 --> 00:01:19,537
Are you officially confirming it?

11
00:01:19,621 --> 00:01:21,081
Are the rumors true?

12
00:01:21,164 --> 00:01:22,832
- Is it true?
- Do you acknowledge it?

13
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:26,127
Oh. It's Seong Huiju!

14
00:01:51,194 --> 00:01:54,072
Prepare yourself to become
the Grand Prince's wife.

15
00:01:57,075 --> 00:01:58,076
You will be up against…

16
00:02:01,746 --> 00:02:03,540
…the whole nation.

17
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:18,513
Before all that,

18
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:21,558
shall we see what you can do?

19
00:02:28,523 --> 00:02:29,524
Well then,

20
00:02:30,483 --> 00:02:32,569
how about a generous donation
to the Crown?

21
00:02:32,652 --> 00:02:33,945
Sway public opinion first.

22
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:37,282
The palace will remain silent.

23
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:47,625
You had me worried for a second.

24
00:02:56,050 --> 00:02:57,385
Move faster already.

25
00:02:57,468 --> 00:03:00,013
{\an8}GRAND PRINCE I-AN ENTERS PALACE
WITH CEO SEONG HUIJU

26
00:03:00,096 --> 00:03:04,017
<i>Today, I'm going to show you the trending
"Seong Huiju makeup" tutorial,</i>

27
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,894
<i>the look that stole Prince I-AN's heart.</i>

28
00:03:09,147 --> 00:03:11,524
"COMMONER" SEONG HUIJU ENTERS PALACE
WHAT'S NEXT?

29
00:03:32,045 --> 00:03:35,673
PERFECT CROWN

30
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:39,510
{\an8}EPISODE 3

31
00:03:46,726 --> 00:03:48,061
{\an8}Welcome, Your Royal Highness.

32
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:51,064
{\an8}Her Majesty is looking for you.

33
00:03:51,981 --> 00:03:54,400
{\an8}- I will pay her a visit tomorrow.
- Your Royal Highness.

34
00:03:54,484 --> 00:03:57,445
{\an8}Her Majesty has even postponed
her meal and is waiting.

35
00:03:58,488 --> 00:04:00,240
{\an8}The matter seems rather urgent.

36
00:04:01,241 --> 00:04:02,492
{\an8}Perhaps you can see her now.

37
00:04:06,579 --> 00:04:08,081
Wait for me. I shall be back.

38
00:04:10,208 --> 00:04:11,542
By myself?

39
00:04:26,766 --> 00:04:27,767
Are you afraid?

40
00:04:28,935 --> 00:04:29,936
No.

41
00:04:31,479 --> 00:04:33,273
Take a nap if you are tired.

42
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:35,608
Okay.

43
00:05:02,093 --> 00:05:04,095
He's even a good actor.

44
00:05:14,522 --> 00:05:17,900
NOT PRIVY TO CEO'S PRIVATE LIFE,
A CAUSE FOR CELEBRATION IF TRUE

45
00:05:17,984 --> 00:05:19,319
Your Majesty.

46
00:05:19,402 --> 00:05:20,987
Grand Prince I-AN has arrived.

47
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,708
Is such a delay necessary?

48
00:05:34,876 --> 00:05:36,836
- I did not know you were looking for me.
- Not that.

49
00:05:37,712 --> 00:05:40,089
I ask whether such a delay is necessary

50
00:05:40,173 --> 00:05:43,885
before you offer an apology
for causing such a scandal.

51
00:05:46,304 --> 00:05:47,305
I see.

52
00:05:48,556 --> 00:05:51,059
I hear you brought that maiden with you.

53
00:05:51,142 --> 00:05:53,061
I understand the need to align stories,

54
00:05:53,561 --> 00:05:56,105
but did you have to bring her
all the way to the palace?

55
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:58,191
Have you any intention

56
00:05:59,442 --> 00:06:00,985
of denying it?

57
00:06:03,363 --> 00:06:04,530
It appears I do not.

58
00:06:06,115 --> 00:06:07,367
I plan to confirm

59
00:06:08,451 --> 00:06:11,704
both the tryst at the hotel
and the possibility of marriage.

60
00:06:14,707 --> 00:06:16,459
Are you throwing a tantrum?

61
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:19,587
Premarital pregnancy…

62
00:06:23,883 --> 00:06:25,176
You can rest assured

63
00:06:25,802 --> 00:06:27,512
that no such tantrum will be thrown.

64
00:06:38,898 --> 00:06:41,401
Your Royal Highness,
Public Affairs has reached out.

65
00:06:42,110 --> 00:06:43,236
What are you doing here?

66
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:45,863
- Pardon?
- You should be guarding Anhwadang Hall.

67
00:06:47,115 --> 00:06:48,449
To keep an eye on Seong Huiju.

68
00:06:49,367 --> 00:06:50,493
But…

69
00:06:50,576 --> 00:06:51,661
My apologies.

70
00:07:02,088 --> 00:07:03,297
Seong Huiju.

71
00:07:03,381 --> 00:07:04,757
Oh. You're here.

72
00:07:04,841 --> 00:07:06,259
Uncle.

73
00:07:08,511 --> 00:07:10,138
See, I told you it'd be spicy.

74
00:07:10,221 --> 00:07:11,764
Have some water.

75
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:12,890
I am fine.

76
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:24,986
Your Majesty,
what are you doing here at this late hour?

77
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:27,738
He said he was having trouble sleeping...

78
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:28,948
I did not ask you.

79
00:07:30,324 --> 00:07:32,452
I was having trouble sleeping.

80
00:07:38,958 --> 00:07:40,418
So I came by.

81
00:07:40,918 --> 00:07:42,420
What does having trouble sleeping

82
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:45,423
have to do with this?

83
00:07:46,424 --> 00:07:50,094
She said a full belly
would help me fall asleep.

84
00:08:01,105 --> 00:08:02,398
Come in, Court Lady Jung.

85
00:08:11,199 --> 00:08:12,200
Your Majesty.

86
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:15,912
Shall I escort you
to Queen Mother's quarters?

87
00:08:25,838 --> 00:08:28,007
You couldn't just let him
finish it in peace?

88
00:08:32,386 --> 00:08:34,055
I mean, come on.

89
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:37,308
A bowl of <i>ramyeon</i>
wouldn't have taken that long to finish.

90
00:08:41,187 --> 00:08:42,688
And if he suffers indigestion?

91
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:44,857
You would be wholly to blame.

92
00:08:45,691 --> 00:08:47,610
And if Queen Mother is angered?

93
00:08:48,194 --> 00:08:50,238
All that over a measly bowl of <i>ramyeon</i>?

94
00:08:50,321 --> 00:08:51,364
The Queen Mother…

95
00:08:53,658 --> 00:08:54,659
denied the request.

96
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:03,626
Well…

97
00:09:04,126 --> 00:09:05,628
we expected as much.

98
00:09:06,212 --> 00:09:08,464
But you know, it still doesn't feel great.

99
00:09:08,548 --> 00:09:10,174
Like I'm being bullied by my in-laws.

100
00:09:10,258 --> 00:09:12,093
Wait! Hold on a second.

101
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:15,012
What will you do
if my in-laws really bully me?

102
00:09:16,055 --> 00:09:18,849
I mean, just look at
how things are unfolding already.

103
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:21,978
Let's say the Queen Mother
and I got into a fight.

104
00:09:22,061 --> 00:09:24,063
Would you take my side?

105
00:09:26,899 --> 00:09:29,652
Why aren't you answering?

106
00:09:30,444 --> 00:09:32,572
Will you take their side and not mine

107
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:34,198
because they're your family?

108
00:09:39,745 --> 00:09:40,871
I will take your side.

109
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:50,381
I must appear

110
00:09:51,591 --> 00:09:52,883
insanely infatuated with you…

111
00:10:01,934 --> 00:10:03,644
…for people to believe

112
00:10:05,521 --> 00:10:07,148
this absurd marriage is genuine.

113
00:10:16,741 --> 00:10:17,825
<i>No, Your Royal Highness.</i>

114
00:10:17,908 --> 00:10:19,910
You cannot let her sleep
in Anhwadang Hall.

115
00:10:19,994 --> 00:10:21,912
We have no choice
with the palace gates shut.

116
00:10:21,996 --> 00:10:24,081
We have the quarters
of the palace attendants.

117
00:10:24,165 --> 00:10:25,666
But she is not a palace attendant.

118
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:28,461
I shall look for other vacant quarters...

119
00:10:28,544 --> 00:10:29,545
No need.

120
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:31,881
Get her a change of clothes as well.

121
00:10:33,049 --> 00:10:34,050
Clothes?

122
00:10:36,469 --> 00:10:39,472
Can I get something that's 100% cotton?

123
00:10:42,016 --> 00:10:44,143
My skin's a little sensitive.

124
00:10:58,074 --> 00:10:59,867
Will you not even consider the sofa?

125
00:11:00,368 --> 00:11:03,079
No. This is perfectly fine.

126
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:09,960
The sofa would be perfectly fine too.

127
00:11:10,044 --> 00:11:13,506
Then you should go. That'd be perfect.

128
00:11:53,045 --> 00:11:54,046
Stop!

129
00:11:59,593 --> 00:12:00,845
My goodness.

130
00:12:06,475 --> 00:12:08,227
- Oh, my.
- Your Royal Highness.

131
00:12:09,478 --> 00:12:10,688
Your Royal Highness!

132
00:12:10,771 --> 00:12:12,022
Stay still!

133
00:12:15,568 --> 00:12:17,027
Your Royal Highness.

134
00:12:19,447 --> 00:12:21,532
- Your Royal Highness!
- What? Stay still…

135
00:12:23,451 --> 00:12:24,744
My goodness.

136
00:12:24,827 --> 00:12:26,829
Do you know what time it is right now?

137
00:12:27,538 --> 00:12:29,707
It's unlike you to sleep in like this.

138
00:12:35,087 --> 00:12:37,381
Ms. Seong is already on her way to work.

139
00:12:37,465 --> 00:12:39,091
With a pep in her step, at that.

140
00:12:59,236 --> 00:13:00,821
You didn't change?

141
00:13:01,405 --> 00:13:02,573
No. Something wrong?

142
00:13:09,997 --> 00:13:12,541
Are you trying to show off
that you spent the night out?

143
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:14,084
Did you not have time to change?

144
00:13:14,585 --> 00:13:17,004
I did have the time, but had no desire to.

145
00:13:17,671 --> 00:13:19,006
I wanted people to know

146
00:13:20,257 --> 00:13:21,509
I didn't go home last night.

147
00:13:22,968 --> 00:13:24,011
Oh.

148
00:13:38,567 --> 00:13:40,319
Are you quite pleased?

149
00:13:41,111 --> 00:13:44,532
Yes, I much prefer this over <i>yakgwa.</i>

150
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:51,872
Did you sleep well last night?

151
00:13:58,212 --> 00:14:01,799
Did you dream about the late king again?

152
00:14:23,737 --> 00:14:25,114
I am afraid.

153
00:14:27,741 --> 00:14:29,910
Do not worry,
Your Highness the Crown Prince.

154
00:14:30,703 --> 00:14:33,664
- You will have me by your side...
- You cannot, Your Royal Highness.

155
00:14:42,131 --> 00:14:43,132
Your Royal Highness.

156
00:14:44,091 --> 00:14:46,302
- The wedding rites are about to commence.
- So?

157
00:14:46,385 --> 00:14:48,929
You should take your place out there.

158
00:14:52,558 --> 00:14:54,560
Should His Majesty learn of this…

159
00:14:58,314 --> 00:15:01,442
you will be punished
for dishonoring the Crown Prince.

160
00:15:01,525 --> 00:15:03,235
Are you prepared for that?

161
00:15:05,863 --> 00:15:06,864
Your Royal Highness!

162
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:12,953
I clearly gave you a chance.

163
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:15,831
Whatever happens from here on…

164
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:19,251
you will have to…

165
00:15:21,128 --> 00:15:22,379
deal with it yourself.

166
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:29,428
<i>I am scared.</i>

167
00:15:32,473 --> 00:15:35,476
Ah. Do not worry, Your Majesty.

168
00:15:35,976 --> 00:15:40,105
You will always have
your grandfather by your side.

169
00:15:43,025 --> 00:15:44,026
Go on.

170
00:15:56,956 --> 00:15:58,791
FAMILY APPRECIATION
MONTH EVENT REPORT

171
00:16:20,521 --> 00:16:22,481
A ROYAL SCANDAL?
SEONG HUIJU HIT THE JACKPOT…

172
00:16:23,732 --> 00:16:27,444
{\an8}"A royal child out of wedlock?
That's insane."

173
00:16:28,278 --> 00:16:30,531
That's right. It's totally insane.

174
00:16:31,865 --> 00:16:34,618
{\an8}"Prince I-AN and Seong Huiju
make a terrible couple."

175
00:16:34,702 --> 00:16:37,204
No, we totally make the hottest couple.

176
00:16:38,831 --> 00:16:40,708
Can you stop reading the comments?

177
00:16:40,791 --> 00:16:42,793
Why? I need to monitor
the situation closely.

178
00:16:43,585 --> 00:16:45,921
{\an8}"Guys, maybe she has something on him?

179
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:48,841
{\an8}Why else would he date a commoner?"

180
00:16:48,924 --> 00:16:50,592
Why do you think, loser?

181
00:16:50,676 --> 00:16:52,845
Because I'm worth dating. That's why.

182
00:16:53,512 --> 00:16:55,264
- You little…
- Here.

183
00:16:55,889 --> 00:16:59,518
The top five trending keywords
are all about you.

184
00:16:59,601 --> 00:17:01,979
Your hotel outfit is already sold out.

185
00:17:02,771 --> 00:17:03,772
Really?

186
00:17:05,524 --> 00:17:06,650
Call the PR team.

187
00:17:06,734 --> 00:17:08,694
The PR team? Why?

188
00:17:08,777 --> 00:17:09,778
Why else?

189
00:17:10,446 --> 00:17:13,449
It's time to take back
the number-one spot in sales.

190
00:17:14,575 --> 00:17:16,535
How can you even
think about that right now?

191
00:17:17,828 --> 00:17:19,204
It's marriage, not retirement.

192
00:17:23,667 --> 00:17:25,753
Oh. Jeongwoo?

193
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:27,421
Hello, sir.

194
00:17:28,172 --> 00:17:30,382
- Isn't he so handsome?
- Super handsome!

195
00:17:30,466 --> 00:17:33,093
This is my first time seeing
Prime Minister Min in person.

196
00:17:33,177 --> 00:17:35,304
He looks like a total celebrity.

197
00:17:35,387 --> 00:17:37,097
Right. But what's he doing here?

198
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:38,307
Maybe because of the scandal?

199
00:17:38,390 --> 00:17:40,851
- Oh! That must be...
- Why is no one working?

200
00:17:43,687 --> 00:17:46,148
You're really going to marry him?

201
00:17:46,899 --> 00:17:48,525
- Yeah.
- His Royal Highness?

202
00:17:48,609 --> 00:17:50,027
Yeah.

203
00:17:50,110 --> 00:17:51,737
I thought you two had just met.

204
00:17:52,362 --> 00:17:53,822
Can't you just stick to dating?

205
00:17:53,906 --> 00:17:56,283
But I want to be with him all the time.

206
00:17:57,117 --> 00:17:59,787
- Huiju…
- I want to wake up next to him

207
00:18:00,412 --> 00:18:01,455
every day.

208
00:18:03,999 --> 00:18:06,126
I hear the royal family

209
00:18:06,210 --> 00:18:08,629
wants to marry him off to someone else.

210
00:18:10,714 --> 00:18:14,051
That's why I have to marry him right now.

211
00:18:14,635 --> 00:18:16,053
While you're the Prime Minister.

212
00:18:21,266 --> 00:18:22,601
I need you to get

213
00:18:24,019 --> 00:18:25,020
my marriage approved.

214
00:18:34,404 --> 00:18:37,324
We're planning to invite
the top 300 patrons in the country.

215
00:18:37,908 --> 00:18:40,160
- What are the criteria?
- Your Royal Highness.

216
00:18:54,716 --> 00:18:57,136
The Queen Mother has taken to her sickbed.

217
00:18:57,219 --> 00:18:58,512
All of a sudden?

218
00:18:58,595 --> 00:19:01,056
Perhaps it's a ploy
to prevent an official statement.

219
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:04,143
The palace cannot speak of celebrations
while a royal elder lies ill.

220
00:19:11,316 --> 00:19:12,818
JUNIOR ALUM

221
00:19:14,027 --> 00:19:15,195
Understood. You may leave.

222
00:19:20,909 --> 00:19:22,327
<i>Your Royal Highness!</i>

223
00:19:23,829 --> 00:19:25,455
I hear you fine. Lower your voice.

224
00:19:26,290 --> 00:19:27,416
<i>Did you read the article?</i>

225
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:30,669
Right before it was pulled.

226
00:19:31,461 --> 00:19:33,213
It was taken down at lightning speed.

227
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:35,090
<i>The Queen Mother has been very busy.</i>

228
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:37,176
I guess even nobles can move quickly

229
00:19:37,259 --> 00:19:38,635
when they want to.

230
00:19:42,973 --> 00:19:43,974
<i>Seong Huiju?</i>

231
00:19:44,516 --> 00:19:45,517
Oh?

232
00:19:46,727 --> 00:19:47,978
You sly fox!

233
00:19:48,061 --> 00:19:50,022
You dare try to seduce His Royal Highness!

234
00:19:51,064 --> 00:19:52,691
- "Fox"?
- Yeah, you fox!

235
00:19:53,442 --> 00:19:56,278
- Oh, my gosh!
- Stay away from His Royal Highness!

236
00:19:56,361 --> 00:19:58,906
- Get lost!
- Hey, good job.

237
00:20:00,824 --> 00:20:01,909
Seong Huiju?

238
00:20:01,992 --> 00:20:03,660
Should we? Should we not?

239
00:20:04,328 --> 00:20:05,412
Come here, you brats.

240
00:20:05,495 --> 00:20:08,290
- We could throw them all.
- "Come here, you brats!"

241
00:20:10,417 --> 00:20:11,960
Get over here now!

242
00:20:27,726 --> 00:20:28,727
Your Royal Highness.

243
00:20:31,355 --> 00:20:32,564
What is all that?

244
00:20:32,648 --> 00:20:34,524
Is it not obvious? These are your duties.

245
00:20:34,608 --> 00:20:36,151
- All of it?
- All of it.

246
00:20:38,195 --> 00:20:40,697
- That cannot be true.
- It most certainly is.

247
00:20:40,781 --> 00:20:44,368
These are the duties you are
to carry out on His Majesty's behalf.

248
00:20:45,035 --> 00:20:48,330
These are the Queen Mother's… Goodness.
This stack is quite heavy.

249
00:20:48,413 --> 00:20:51,541
These are the Queen Mother's duties
you are to carry out

250
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:53,543
in her absence.

251
00:20:53,627 --> 00:20:56,338
And these are your duties
that accumulated while you were away.

252
00:20:57,005 --> 00:20:58,715
- You got this.
- Get out.

253
00:20:58,799 --> 00:21:00,092
Yes, sir.

254
00:21:00,676 --> 00:21:02,719
Let's go. Off we go.

255
00:21:06,848 --> 00:21:10,102
You little brats should be in school
with your noses in books.

256
00:21:10,185 --> 00:21:11,687
Eyes down!

257
00:21:12,896 --> 00:21:15,482
Does Prince I-AN put food on your table?

258
00:21:15,565 --> 00:21:17,693
He may not feed us, but he gives us money.

259
00:21:17,776 --> 00:21:20,195
- Right.
- We're royal scholarship students.

260
00:21:20,988 --> 00:21:22,948
That money was for your studies.

261
00:21:23,031 --> 00:21:26,159
Do you think he wanted you to spend
that money buying eggs to throw?

262
00:21:26,827 --> 00:21:27,953
And you, Hyerin.

263
00:21:28,495 --> 00:21:30,706
Why did you assume I seduced him?

264
00:21:30,789 --> 00:21:31,790
Isn't it obvious?

265
00:21:31,873 --> 00:21:33,083
Why, you little…

266
00:21:33,166 --> 00:21:35,919
So young and already full of prejudice.

267
00:21:36,003 --> 00:21:37,879
If I had it my way,

268
00:21:38,630 --> 00:21:42,467
I'd give you hell and take legal action
for pulling something like this…

269
00:21:44,011 --> 00:21:45,178
Come here.

270
00:21:46,305 --> 00:21:47,556
But right now,

271
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:50,559
your big sis here has
a major undertaking ahead of her.

272
00:21:51,226 --> 00:21:53,353
So I'll let it slide just this once.

273
00:21:54,062 --> 00:21:55,063
Got it?

274
00:21:56,565 --> 00:21:58,400
- Answer me!
- Yes, ma'am!

275
00:22:01,987 --> 00:22:03,363
Off you go.

276
00:22:03,447 --> 00:22:04,823
<i>Almighty God.</i>

277
00:22:05,991 --> 00:22:08,160
Please have mercy on us,

278
00:22:09,161 --> 00:22:10,787
forgive us our sins,

279
00:22:11,872 --> 00:22:15,542
and bring us to everlasting life.

280
00:22:17,044 --> 00:22:18,045
Amen.

281
00:22:21,840 --> 00:22:23,091
Amen.

282
00:22:25,302 --> 00:22:27,387
You said you couldn't come for a while.

283
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:31,808
I heard my friend is getting married,
so I came to pray.

284
00:22:33,143 --> 00:22:36,438
That friend is very lucky to have you
praying for her happiness.

285
00:22:37,022 --> 00:22:38,023
I'm not so sure.

286
00:22:38,982 --> 00:22:40,317
I prayed for something sinful.

287
00:22:41,818 --> 00:22:42,986
Something sinful?

288
00:22:44,905 --> 00:22:46,114
I do not feel inclined

289
00:22:47,032 --> 00:22:48,367
to congratulate her.

290
00:23:01,254 --> 00:23:03,924
<i>But I don't want to stop her either.</i>

291
00:23:10,097 --> 00:23:11,640
<i>Even if I don't think it's right…</i>

292
00:23:12,557 --> 00:23:13,975
Damn it.

293
00:23:14,059 --> 00:23:16,228
Where did that punk hide it?

294
00:23:16,812 --> 00:23:18,522
<i>If that's what she wants…</i>

295
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:22,275
- Ma'am.
- Hey, Jeongwoo.

296
00:23:22,359 --> 00:23:23,735
Are you running an errand?

297
00:23:23,819 --> 00:23:26,321
Yes.

298
00:23:26,405 --> 00:23:28,323
Principal Kim was looking for you earlier.

299
00:23:28,407 --> 00:23:29,658
Did you see him?

300
00:23:30,659 --> 00:23:31,868
<i>…I have to let her.</i>

301
00:23:32,577 --> 00:23:33,787
Found it.

302
00:23:36,498 --> 00:23:37,499
Got it.

303
00:24:04,526 --> 00:24:07,737
I mean, how did those brats
even get past security?

304
00:24:08,655 --> 00:24:11,450
You have to hand it
to the high schoolers in this country.

305
00:24:20,917 --> 00:24:21,918
Father?

306
00:24:34,097 --> 00:24:37,142
Can I get you anything?

307
00:24:40,187 --> 00:24:41,354
Don't bother. Sit.

308
00:24:50,238 --> 00:24:51,656
About that scandal…

309
00:24:51,740 --> 00:24:53,408
No need to explain.

310
00:24:54,868 --> 00:24:58,705
- You're not curious?
- There's nothing to be curious about.

311
00:24:58,788 --> 00:24:59,789
I'm sure

312
00:25:00,290 --> 00:25:02,584
it's just a cheap stunt
you pulled for attention.

313
00:25:05,378 --> 00:25:06,546
Then why are you here?

314
00:25:11,134 --> 00:25:12,135
It's nearly…

315
00:25:13,637 --> 00:25:15,180
Taeju's mother's death anniversary.

316
00:25:17,015 --> 00:25:18,934
I was wondering if you even remembered.

317
00:25:22,646 --> 00:25:23,647
Ma'am.

318
00:25:27,817 --> 00:25:30,028
She's been standing
outside the house for hours,

319
00:25:30,654 --> 00:25:32,489
but she refuses to talk.

320
00:25:33,073 --> 00:25:36,076
Then you should've reported her
to the police, not brought her inside.

321
00:25:36,701 --> 00:25:37,827
Send her away.

322
00:25:37,911 --> 00:25:40,830
How can we just send away a child
in the middle of the night?

323
00:25:43,083 --> 00:25:45,669
Little one, are you lost?

324
00:25:48,213 --> 00:25:49,381
What's your name?

325
00:25:53,593 --> 00:25:55,011
You don't want to say?

326
00:25:58,348 --> 00:25:59,683
I am

327
00:26:00,267 --> 00:26:01,935
Lee Jooyeon's daughter.

328
00:26:07,566 --> 00:26:08,733
You're my dad…

329
00:26:09,651 --> 00:26:10,652
aren't you?

330
00:26:23,915 --> 00:26:25,709
- Honey! Honey!
- Mom!

331
00:26:25,792 --> 00:26:28,044
- Ma'am! Wake up, ma'am!
- Honey!

332
00:26:28,128 --> 00:26:30,422
- Honey!
- Ma'am!

333
00:26:30,964 --> 00:26:33,133
- Ma'am! Oh, dear goodness!
- Mom, wake up!

334
00:26:33,216 --> 00:26:35,719
<i>Since the day your mother abandoned you…</i>

335
00:26:35,802 --> 00:26:37,095
- Ma'am.
- Mommy!

336
00:26:37,178 --> 00:26:38,972
<i>…our lives fell into despair.</i>

337
00:26:46,980 --> 00:26:48,440
CERTIFICATE OF AWARD

338
00:26:48,523 --> 00:26:50,817
Buy me a bike too.

339
00:26:50,900 --> 00:26:53,570
The same one as Taeju.

340
00:26:56,197 --> 00:26:58,533
<i>You dared to be greedy…</i>

341
00:26:59,117 --> 00:27:00,327
REPORT CARD

342
00:27:01,328 --> 00:27:02,996
I want a building too.

343
00:27:03,079 --> 00:27:04,914
One that's taller than Taeju's.

344
00:27:04,998 --> 00:27:06,249
<i>So greedy…</i>

345
00:27:07,250 --> 00:27:08,251
STOCK PRICE ANALYSIS

346
00:27:08,335 --> 00:27:10,003
Amend your will, Father.

347
00:27:10,670 --> 00:27:11,921
In my favor.

348
00:27:12,005 --> 00:27:13,632
<i>Your greed was relentless!</i>

349
00:27:20,305 --> 00:27:22,057
Keep your hands off the company.

350
00:27:22,140 --> 00:27:23,183
And if I don't?

351
00:27:23,266 --> 00:27:24,893
I'll have no choice but to act.

352
00:27:26,811 --> 00:27:28,980
- What? Are you going to disown me?
- Why not?

353
00:27:29,064 --> 00:27:30,273
Listen, Mr. Seong Hyeonguk.

354
00:27:30,357 --> 00:27:32,108
You dare call your father by his name?

355
00:27:32,192 --> 00:27:33,693
You just said you'd disown me.

356
00:27:34,527 --> 00:27:36,112
Then you wouldn't be my dad anyway.

357
00:27:37,614 --> 00:27:40,492
So, Mr. Seong Hyeonguk, to summarize,

358
00:27:40,575 --> 00:27:42,077
I shouldn't bother acting out

359
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:45,163
because it'll all be
Taeju's in the end, right?

360
00:27:45,664 --> 00:27:47,415
Seong Taeju will be the ultimate winner.

361
00:27:47,499 --> 00:27:49,542
Taeju is so awesome!

362
00:27:50,043 --> 00:27:51,252
That's the gist.

363
00:27:51,920 --> 00:27:52,921
Right?

364
00:27:53,880 --> 00:27:56,800
I should just kill Taeju
and secure my spot in hell.

365
00:27:56,883 --> 00:27:57,967
Seong Huiju!

366
00:27:58,051 --> 00:28:00,929
Anyone who ever tried to pick a fight
with me was exactly like you.

367
00:28:01,721 --> 00:28:04,140
They'd stack the deck
so they couldn't help but win,

368
00:28:04,224 --> 00:28:06,351
and put me in a spot
where I was bound to lose.

369
00:28:08,103 --> 00:28:09,437
I guess they weren't confident

370
00:28:10,063 --> 00:28:11,523
they could win on equal terms.

371
00:28:16,152 --> 00:28:17,153
But you know what?

372
00:28:17,654 --> 00:28:18,988
It's fine.

373
00:28:19,614 --> 00:28:21,366
I'm used to going up against

374
00:28:22,450 --> 00:28:23,493
people like that.

375
00:28:23,576 --> 00:28:24,994
You just won't quit.

376
00:28:25,078 --> 00:28:26,079
I wish you…

377
00:28:26,955 --> 00:28:27,956
all the best.

378
00:28:29,374 --> 00:28:30,917
Though I'm sure you'll lose anyway.

379
00:29:07,579 --> 00:29:09,748
PRINCE

380
00:29:21,050 --> 00:29:22,594
Sorry for hanging up on you earlier...

381
00:29:22,677 --> 00:29:23,928
<i>Are you okay?</i>

382
00:29:27,432 --> 00:29:28,600
<i>Are you all right?</i>

383
00:29:32,103 --> 00:29:33,897
<i>Seong Huiju, can you not hear me?</i>

384
00:29:35,940 --> 00:29:37,776
Can I call you back tomorrow?

385
00:29:38,693 --> 00:29:39,694
<i>What?</i>

386
00:29:40,403 --> 00:29:41,738
I'm a little busy right now.

387
00:29:43,072 --> 00:29:44,157
I'll call you tomorrow.

388
00:29:59,881 --> 00:30:02,133
JUNIOR ALUM

389
00:30:43,508 --> 00:30:46,010
CERTIFICATE OF AWARD

390
00:30:59,107 --> 00:31:00,108
HAPPY BIRTHDAY, TAEJU

391
00:31:00,191 --> 00:31:01,818
HOPE YOU GROW UP
STRONG AND HEALTHY

392
00:31:08,575 --> 00:31:10,577
Buy me a bike too.

393
00:31:11,578 --> 00:31:13,955
The same one as Taeju.

394
00:31:29,137 --> 00:31:30,597
REPORT CARD

395
00:31:37,312 --> 00:31:38,730
I want a building too.

396
00:31:39,647 --> 00:31:41,024
One that's taller than Taeju's.

397
00:31:48,323 --> 00:31:49,991
Amend your will, Father.

398
00:31:50,575 --> 00:31:51,826
In my favor.

399
00:32:08,885 --> 00:32:09,969
Who is it?

400
00:32:13,848 --> 00:32:15,183
Someone lost their damn mind.

401
00:32:15,767 --> 00:32:17,310
Who the hell is it at this hour…

402
00:32:21,105 --> 00:32:22,273
Damn it.

403
00:32:31,074 --> 00:32:36,788
<i>Teatime for His Royal Highness!</i>

404
00:32:37,914 --> 00:32:38,915
Your Royal Highness?

405
00:32:39,624 --> 00:32:41,709
Wait, are we playing hide and seek?

406
00:32:43,711 --> 00:32:44,796
What are you doing here?

407
00:32:44,879 --> 00:32:46,631
Wait, are you allowed to be here?

408
00:32:46,714 --> 00:32:49,217
Hold on. Did anyone see you?

409
00:32:49,300 --> 00:32:50,426
Where's Aide Choi?

410
00:32:51,135 --> 00:32:52,303
You play baseball at home?

411
00:32:56,599 --> 00:33:00,269
I have one too many enemies, you see.

412
00:33:05,650 --> 00:33:06,651
Oh.

413
00:33:06,734 --> 00:33:07,735
Wait.

414
00:33:08,361 --> 00:33:11,197
How did you even get here?

415
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:12,907
Wait, did you come here alone?

416
00:33:12,991 --> 00:33:13,992
Yeah.

417
00:33:15,118 --> 00:33:16,494
You can't just…

418
00:33:21,874 --> 00:33:23,084
Let me get this straight.

419
00:33:24,210 --> 00:33:25,962
You picked these up yourself?

420
00:33:37,932 --> 00:33:39,017
THE SEONG HUIJU COMBO

421
00:33:39,100 --> 00:33:40,309
I will have this one.

422
00:33:42,270 --> 00:33:43,896
Yes, Your Royal Highness.

423
00:33:45,106 --> 00:33:47,066
<i>"Seduce the Prince" Seong Huiju Combo.</i>

424
00:33:48,026 --> 00:33:49,027
It seemed popular.

425
00:34:11,716 --> 00:34:12,717
Seriously?

426
00:34:13,217 --> 00:34:16,220
Couldn't you have left
after you finished your work?

427
00:34:25,605 --> 00:34:27,565
- What is it?
- Just a bit amazed.

428
00:34:28,357 --> 00:34:29,484
By what?

429
00:34:30,276 --> 00:34:31,819
I came because you sounded so down.

430
00:34:32,612 --> 00:34:35,364
But seeing you eat,
you seem perfectly fine.

431
00:34:41,162 --> 00:34:42,288
I was a little down.

432
00:34:42,371 --> 00:34:45,416
I was dragged
through the mud all day, you see.

433
00:34:46,375 --> 00:34:48,961
I was barraged
with hate comments on social media.

434
00:34:49,045 --> 00:34:51,547
My father suddenly threatened
to disown me.

435
00:34:51,631 --> 00:34:52,632
Oh, that's right.

436
00:34:53,132 --> 00:34:56,636
I even got egged by your fans today.

437
00:34:56,719 --> 00:34:59,347
I totally forgot to ask
if those eggs were antibiotic-free.

438
00:35:00,014 --> 00:35:01,182
You got "egged"?

439
00:35:01,265 --> 00:35:02,767
Yeah. Two eggs, no less.

440
00:35:02,850 --> 00:35:06,187
Those little pip-squeaks were
so damn strong for no reason.

441
00:35:07,271 --> 00:35:08,689
- It still hurts.
- Here?

442
00:35:08,773 --> 00:35:10,274
Yeah. Just downstairs.

443
00:35:12,026 --> 00:35:13,611
Are you hurt?

444
00:35:17,115 --> 00:35:18,157
Are you hurt anywhere?

445
00:35:53,985 --> 00:35:55,403
An investigation is required.

446
00:36:00,616 --> 00:36:01,951
They're coming right now?

447
00:36:02,034 --> 00:36:03,619
That's what I said. Now, move it!

448
00:36:11,544 --> 00:36:13,546
She will be staying here
for the time being.

449
00:36:20,469 --> 00:36:22,972
She has been receiving
a troublesome amount of attention.

450
00:36:24,056 --> 00:36:25,349
I was concerned.

451
00:36:26,100 --> 00:36:27,226
So you were…

452
00:36:28,352 --> 00:36:29,937
concerned.

453
00:36:30,730 --> 00:36:31,814
And my instructions?

454
00:36:31,898 --> 00:36:34,150
Everything is ready, Your Royal Highness.

455
00:36:41,032 --> 00:36:42,033
Oh!

456
00:36:49,165 --> 00:36:50,750
Maybe that's a bit too close?

457
00:37:05,640 --> 00:37:07,558
Please make yourself at home.

458
00:37:09,018 --> 00:37:11,479
What should I call you?

459
00:37:12,271 --> 00:37:13,856
- Pardon?
- How should I address you?

460
00:37:17,735 --> 00:37:20,863
I am Yeongmun of the Kim Family,
the steward of this residence.

461
00:37:20,947 --> 00:37:23,824
Feel free to call me Steward Kim.

462
00:37:25,201 --> 00:37:27,078
Steward? Hmm.

463
00:37:27,912 --> 00:37:28,913
Yes, ma'am.

464
00:37:29,622 --> 00:37:30,706
Steward.

465
00:37:32,667 --> 00:37:34,585
It's late, so I will leave you to rest.

466
00:37:34,669 --> 00:37:38,339
I will give you a proper tour
of the property tomorrow.

467
00:37:38,422 --> 00:37:39,674
All right.

468
00:37:45,179 --> 00:37:46,305
Just a second.

469
00:37:47,640 --> 00:37:51,185
How shall I address you?

470
00:37:57,900 --> 00:38:01,779
I prefer Ms. Seong or Executive Director,
but you can call me by my name.

471
00:38:01,862 --> 00:38:04,365
You're not my employee, after all.

472
00:38:07,159 --> 00:38:08,160
Then, I shall

473
00:38:09,161 --> 00:38:10,454
address you as Your Ladyship.

474
00:38:11,998 --> 00:38:13,666
"Your Ladyship"?

475
00:38:14,875 --> 00:38:16,043
Well then.

476
00:38:27,013 --> 00:38:28,806
I was at the palace yesterday,

477
00:38:28,889 --> 00:38:31,225
and today, the prince's private residence.

478
00:38:40,568 --> 00:38:41,819
Yes, Your Royal Highness.

479
00:38:42,403 --> 00:38:43,571
<i>Do you like your room?</i>

480
00:38:44,905 --> 00:38:45,906
I mean, it's nice.

481
00:38:46,407 --> 00:38:48,409
It feels like I'm on
a historical drama set.

482
00:38:49,618 --> 00:38:51,287
Why aren't you sleeping?

483
00:38:51,829 --> 00:38:52,955
<i>I have some work to do.</i>

484
00:38:55,958 --> 00:38:57,209
Do you want me to help?

485
00:39:52,306 --> 00:39:54,892
So am I really going to live here now?

486
00:39:56,352 --> 00:39:58,104
Well, it's just that

487
00:39:58,646 --> 00:40:01,065
I'm quite an independent woman.

488
00:40:01,565 --> 00:40:03,401
I find this bustling environment…

489
00:40:04,318 --> 00:40:05,694
a bit bothersome, shall I say?

490
00:40:06,195 --> 00:40:07,738
It's so far from work too.

491
00:40:09,532 --> 00:40:11,117
Shouldn't you be more "bothered"

492
00:40:11,867 --> 00:40:15,287
if I were to leave you in harm's way
when I'm supposedly infatuated with you?

493
00:40:15,371 --> 00:40:16,580
Commute aside.

494
00:40:16,664 --> 00:40:18,290
Okay.

495
00:40:24,422 --> 00:40:25,464
By the way…

496
00:40:27,216 --> 00:40:28,509
You wanted to help.

497
00:40:28,592 --> 00:40:29,593
Is this you helping?

498
00:40:30,511 --> 00:40:32,888
I don't know anything
about the royal ancestral rites.

499
00:40:33,389 --> 00:40:35,349
I've never even attended
any of my family's.

500
00:40:43,941 --> 00:40:45,234
What do you want to know?

501
00:40:47,987 --> 00:40:49,155
Why are you marrying me?

502
00:40:50,698 --> 00:40:52,908
Isn't it a bit late to be asking that?

503
00:40:52,992 --> 00:40:55,494
We only made the decision yesterday.

504
00:40:55,578 --> 00:40:57,788
Why can't I be a little curious today?

505
00:40:59,707 --> 00:41:00,791
You have a lot of money.

506
00:41:01,459 --> 00:41:03,210
The richest in the country, no less.

507
00:41:05,546 --> 00:41:07,006
Is that your reason?

508
00:41:07,089 --> 00:41:08,424
The most important reason.

509
00:41:08,507 --> 00:41:11,093
It would help the royal family,
always under fire

510
00:41:11,177 --> 00:41:13,095
for squandering taxpayers' money.

511
00:41:15,097 --> 00:41:16,891
And what a noble reason it is.

512
00:41:17,391 --> 00:41:18,893
Second.

513
00:41:21,896 --> 00:41:22,938
Beauty.

514
00:41:23,939 --> 00:41:24,982
"Beauty"?

515
00:41:25,566 --> 00:41:28,360
Oh, I guess that finally broke through.

516
00:41:30,404 --> 00:41:31,989
- Third.
- What? What now?

517
00:41:32,072 --> 00:41:33,657
Because my family doesn't overstep?

518
00:41:33,741 --> 00:41:35,784
If I say I wish to ascend the throne,

519
00:41:37,995 --> 00:41:40,122
all would condemn me and hurl insults.

520
00:41:44,460 --> 00:41:45,461
But I believe

521
00:41:46,712 --> 00:41:47,922
you would understand me.

522
00:42:11,987 --> 00:42:14,323
{\an8}The Inner Court Banquet
is still some time away.

523
00:42:14,406 --> 00:42:17,159
{\an8}Yet I am already being pressed
to make a decision.

524
00:42:17,243 --> 00:42:19,203
{\an8}It appears they are quite anxious,

525
00:42:19,286 --> 00:42:21,413
as they need to finalize
the guest list soon.

526
00:42:21,497 --> 00:42:25,084
Does Your Majesty have any criteria
in mind for the guest list?

527
00:42:25,668 --> 00:42:26,794
I'm not sure.

528
00:42:30,214 --> 00:42:33,425
Those with exemplary character,
admirable talents,

529
00:42:34,969 --> 00:42:36,387
and innate nobility?

530
00:42:39,390 --> 00:42:41,100
Would that suffice?

531
00:42:51,402 --> 00:42:53,320
I must cancel today's itinerary.

532
00:42:54,154 --> 00:42:55,364
Pardon?

533
00:42:55,447 --> 00:42:56,574
But they already...

534
00:42:56,657 --> 00:42:58,075
Surely there should be no issue.

535
00:43:01,287 --> 00:43:02,997
I am indisposed, after all.

536
00:43:18,387 --> 00:43:20,264
Your Ladyship, please wake up.

537
00:43:25,311 --> 00:43:26,604
Your Ladyship, wake up.

538
00:43:28,272 --> 00:43:29,273
Wait, hold on.

539
00:43:31,025 --> 00:43:33,319
How dare you storm in here! Hey, you!

540
00:43:33,402 --> 00:43:34,486
Youngseon!

541
00:43:34,570 --> 00:43:36,947
Why that little prick…

542
00:43:39,116 --> 00:43:40,284
What in the world?

543
00:43:52,671 --> 00:43:53,672
What's this about?

544
00:43:53,756 --> 00:43:57,468
Cooperate with the Junghwajeon Hall
fire investigation, please.

545
00:43:57,551 --> 00:43:58,969
"Cooperate"?

546
00:44:02,640 --> 00:44:04,016
At the Royal Birthday Banquet,

547
00:44:04,892 --> 00:44:07,645
you entered a restricted area
of the palace, didn't you?

548
00:44:08,771 --> 00:44:10,731
I did get lost at one point.

549
00:44:11,649 --> 00:44:12,650
But what about it?

550
00:44:13,400 --> 00:44:15,778
Are you suggesting
I started the fire or something?

551
00:44:16,362 --> 00:44:17,821
Nothing has been ruled out yet.

552
00:44:18,989 --> 00:44:22,618
You'll need to give a detailed account
of what you did and who you met there.

553
00:44:23,369 --> 00:44:25,204
What exactly am I supposed to explain?

554
00:44:29,124 --> 00:44:30,668
What was that?

555
00:44:30,751 --> 00:44:31,752
You stay here.

556
00:44:32,503 --> 00:44:34,963
You've publicly stated,
"The royal family is a money pit.

557
00:44:35,464 --> 00:44:38,592
Someone should abolish the Crown.
Let's bring out the guillotine."

558
00:44:39,134 --> 00:44:40,135
Is that correct?

559
00:44:43,889 --> 00:44:44,890
Do you have a warrant?

560
00:44:47,184 --> 00:44:50,145
Under the Royalty
and Specialist Protection Law,

561
00:44:50,229 --> 00:44:53,649
suspects of royal threats
may be investigated prior to a warrant.

562
00:44:54,817 --> 00:44:55,859
Get started.

563
00:44:56,819 --> 00:44:58,612
Hold on. Take your shoes off.

564
00:44:59,780 --> 00:45:01,323
No, you can't take that!

565
00:45:07,496 --> 00:45:09,540
What do you think you're doing?

566
00:45:09,623 --> 00:45:11,583
- Hold on a second.
- You can't take this!

567
00:45:11,667 --> 00:45:13,377
- What are you doing?
- Move!

568
00:45:13,460 --> 00:45:16,130
- Is this really necessary?
- Please step aside.

569
00:45:17,589 --> 00:45:18,799
What are you doing?

570
00:45:18,882 --> 00:45:20,843
- This is insane.
- Why are you doing this?

571
00:45:27,891 --> 00:45:29,059
Damn it. What now?

572
00:45:29,143 --> 00:45:30,853
Gosh, you're working so hard.

573
00:45:30,936 --> 00:45:32,020
Have you eaten yet?

574
00:45:32,104 --> 00:45:33,731
- You need to eat something.
- I'm fine.

575
00:45:33,814 --> 00:45:35,482
Let's fill that belly first.

576
00:45:35,566 --> 00:45:39,111
This is His Royal Highness's favorite,
so let's have a taste.

577
00:45:39,194 --> 00:45:40,571
Come on. Take a seat.

578
00:45:40,654 --> 00:45:43,699
Sit down. Let's have a bite while we chat.

579
00:45:44,199 --> 00:45:45,868
Go on. Just try one.

580
00:45:48,912 --> 00:45:52,040
Your Ladyship,
you need to eat something too.

581
00:45:52,124 --> 00:45:53,917
Can't be questioned on an empty stomach.

582
00:45:54,001 --> 00:45:55,794
- Go on. It's still warm.
- No thanks.

583
00:45:55,878 --> 00:45:57,087
- Come on!
- Stop it.

584
00:45:57,671 --> 00:45:59,214
I'm calling His Royal Highness.

585
00:46:01,175 --> 00:46:02,676
Why isn't he picking up?

586
00:46:03,886 --> 00:46:05,137
He probably won't answer.

587
00:46:05,804 --> 00:46:06,805
What?

588
00:46:06,889 --> 00:46:09,308
Cell phones are not allowed
during the ritual.

589
00:46:10,350 --> 00:46:11,351
Ritual?

590
00:46:11,977 --> 00:46:13,061
As in ancestral rites?

591
00:46:34,583 --> 00:46:36,585
<i>Ms. Do. You're running, right?</i>

592
00:46:36,668 --> 00:46:38,504
Yes, I'm running.

593
00:46:38,587 --> 00:46:40,422
What a hell of a way to spend the weekend.

594
00:46:40,506 --> 00:46:42,883
What choice do I have?
You're the only one I can trust.

595
00:46:42,966 --> 00:46:44,301
Forget all that.

596
00:46:44,384 --> 00:46:46,094
Prepare to give me a hefty bonus.

597
00:46:46,678 --> 00:46:47,721
Hang up now.

598
00:46:50,182 --> 00:46:51,183
I got this.

599
00:46:53,060 --> 00:46:54,311
She won't get in.

600
00:46:54,394 --> 00:46:55,771
Why not?

601
00:46:55,854 --> 00:46:57,105
She's a civilian.

602
00:46:57,981 --> 00:47:00,901
Civilians may enter Jongmyo Shrine
only on special days.

603
00:47:02,861 --> 00:47:03,862
Come on.

604
00:47:05,823 --> 00:47:07,950
Oh. Oh!

605
00:47:09,576 --> 00:47:11,745
ROYAL PROTECTION BRANCH

606
00:47:29,429 --> 00:47:30,430
Shall we?

607
00:47:42,150 --> 00:47:43,443
- Hurry up, ma'am.
- Hold on…

608
00:47:44,278 --> 00:47:46,196
My goodness.

609
00:47:47,155 --> 00:47:49,241
Wait. I can't believe this.

610
00:47:49,324 --> 00:47:51,285
- Please let me in this once.
- No, you can't.

611
00:47:51,368 --> 00:47:53,120
I'm from Castle Beauty.

612
00:47:53,203 --> 00:47:54,830
I need to see His Royal Highness.

613
00:47:54,913 --> 00:47:55,998
We already told you no.

614
00:47:56,498 --> 00:47:57,791
Just leave already!

615
00:47:57,875 --> 00:47:59,585
How can I when I know he's in there?

616
00:48:04,131 --> 00:48:05,674
Ms. Do!

617
00:48:06,174 --> 00:48:08,802
Ms. Do!

618
00:48:09,386 --> 00:48:11,763
Ms. Do! Oh, Ms. Do!

619
00:48:11,847 --> 00:48:13,265
Ms. Do…

620
00:48:17,144 --> 00:48:18,812
We come by order of the Grand Prince.

621
00:48:18,896 --> 00:48:21,648
GRAND PRINCE I-AN

622
00:48:41,251 --> 00:48:42,252
Good heavens!

623
00:48:44,755 --> 00:48:45,839
That…

624
00:48:45,923 --> 00:48:47,799
Isn't that the Grand Prince's <i>hopae?</i>

625
00:48:47,883 --> 00:48:49,885
Why was that precious thing in the toilet?

626
00:48:51,511 --> 00:48:53,096
- Steward Kim.
- Yes?

627
00:48:55,891 --> 00:48:57,267
Please take it to Jongmyo.

628
00:48:58,226 --> 00:49:00,479
- Pardon?
- Just in case.

629
00:49:01,855 --> 00:49:02,898
I'm counting on you.

630
00:49:03,607 --> 00:49:04,608
You got this!

631
00:49:07,861 --> 00:49:08,862
Good luck!

632
00:49:10,238 --> 00:49:11,323
Good? Step aside.

633
00:49:11,406 --> 00:49:13,951
I knew it!
You could've just let me pass earlier!

634
00:49:20,666 --> 00:49:22,417
Where are you going? It's this way.

635
00:49:24,044 --> 00:49:25,921
That bonus better be a generous one.

636
00:49:26,672 --> 00:49:27,714
I'm so exhausted.

637
00:50:19,683 --> 00:50:22,144
Oh, dear. He can't step out
while the ritual is underway.

638
00:50:22,227 --> 00:50:24,646
It's already started.

639
00:50:33,113 --> 00:50:34,156
Oh.

640
00:50:35,490 --> 00:50:37,617
- If he can't leave…
- Yes?

641
00:50:38,118 --> 00:50:39,494
…we can go in instead.

642
00:50:40,787 --> 00:50:41,997
What?

643
00:50:55,302 --> 00:50:57,054
- We need to go.
- What?

644
00:50:57,137 --> 00:50:59,139
- We need to go.
- Pardon?

645
00:50:59,222 --> 00:51:00,223
We need to go.

646
00:51:01,058 --> 00:51:02,976
- How did you even get in here?
- Quiet…

647
00:51:04,978 --> 00:51:06,229
We need to go.

648
00:51:07,647 --> 00:51:09,191
We need to go right now.

649
00:51:13,987 --> 00:51:15,197
So…

650
00:51:16,448 --> 00:51:18,325
You're going to question me at the palace?

651
00:51:26,166 --> 00:51:27,292
Seong Huiju!

652
00:51:35,759 --> 00:51:37,135
Mr. Jung.

653
00:51:38,178 --> 00:51:39,429
Your Royal Highness.

654
00:51:40,806 --> 00:51:43,934
I heard the Royal Ancestral Rite
was being held at Jongmyo Shrine today.

655
00:51:44,518 --> 00:51:46,937
- What brings you by?
- His Majesty is presiding over it.

656
00:51:48,772 --> 00:51:50,524
But what business have you here?

657
00:51:51,900 --> 00:51:54,444
Without authorization
from either His Majesty or me.

658
00:51:57,239 --> 00:51:58,782
I gave the authorization.

659
00:52:07,999 --> 00:52:11,128
As I heard the prime suspect
in the arson case had been identified.

660
00:52:11,753 --> 00:52:12,754
And since she is…

661
00:52:15,006 --> 00:52:17,592
considered a flight risk
and may destroy evidence.

662
00:52:19,594 --> 00:52:21,847
But I did not know that you would be here.

663
00:52:23,306 --> 00:52:24,683
Is there actually any evidence?

664
00:52:25,934 --> 00:52:28,395
As if insulting the Crown
with such insolent attire

665
00:52:29,020 --> 00:52:31,731
<i>and threatening others
within the palace were not enough,</i>

666
00:52:32,482 --> 00:52:33,525
I hear she was absent

667
00:52:34,818 --> 00:52:36,486
at the time of the incident.

668
00:52:37,154 --> 00:52:38,780
Does that constitute evidence?

669
00:52:38,864 --> 00:52:40,073
Perhaps not.

670
00:52:40,157 --> 00:52:42,742
But it should be enough to tarnish…

671
00:52:44,452 --> 00:52:45,871
her reputation

672
00:52:46,454 --> 00:52:48,290
or her company's reputation.

673
00:52:48,999 --> 00:52:50,167
Wait, my company?

674
00:52:53,753 --> 00:52:55,088
Then have me questioned too.

675
00:52:58,633 --> 00:53:01,136
Every circumstance
that casts suspicion on her

676
00:53:02,304 --> 00:53:04,139
applies to me as well.

677
00:53:13,690 --> 00:53:15,358
Will your confidence hold?

678
00:53:17,444 --> 00:53:18,570
I wonder

679
00:53:20,614 --> 00:53:21,865
if yours will hold.

680
00:53:36,338 --> 00:53:38,048
Ms. Seong!

681
00:53:41,885 --> 00:53:43,261
Oh, Your Royal Highness!

682
00:53:43,887 --> 00:53:45,138
- Summon a physician.
- I-AN.

683
00:53:47,015 --> 00:53:49,517
Feel free to come to Anhwadang Hall
for the questioning.

684
00:53:52,270 --> 00:53:54,189
Summon a physician!

685
00:53:54,272 --> 00:53:55,523
Hurry.

686
00:53:57,150 --> 00:53:58,526
Are you all right, Ms. Seong?

687
00:54:23,843 --> 00:54:24,844
Open your eyes.

688
00:54:28,014 --> 00:54:29,808
Wow.

689
00:54:30,767 --> 00:54:31,935
Wow, we totally slayed!

690
00:54:32,018 --> 00:54:33,019
Slayed, my foot.

691
00:54:34,437 --> 00:54:35,897
How could you agree to come here?

692
00:54:37,107 --> 00:54:39,901
That Mr. Jung or whatever
practically dragged me out.

693
00:54:39,985 --> 00:54:40,986
How could I resist?

694
00:54:45,573 --> 00:54:46,574
So…

695
00:54:47,617 --> 00:54:49,244
will I be going to prison?

696
00:54:51,413 --> 00:54:52,414
Does that scare you?

697
00:54:53,915 --> 00:54:55,208
Me?

698
00:54:55,292 --> 00:54:57,335
I'm Seong Huiju of Castle Group.

699
00:54:57,419 --> 00:55:00,005
Prosecutor investigations
and search-and-seizure raids…

700
00:55:00,505 --> 00:55:01,506
Stuff like that

701
00:55:02,090 --> 00:55:04,718
is practically an annual event.

702
00:55:06,177 --> 00:55:10,515
I was just wondering which law firm
I should hire this time.

703
00:55:10,598 --> 00:55:12,726
- Is that something to be proud of?
- I mean,

704
00:55:13,393 --> 00:55:14,894
it's nothing to brag about, but...

705
00:55:14,978 --> 00:55:16,980
She won't be able to act for now.

706
00:55:17,063 --> 00:55:18,898
She knows pursuing you would implicate me,

707
00:55:19,399 --> 00:55:20,900
which would only escalate matters.

708
00:55:25,739 --> 00:55:29,200
But wouldn't you say
that was quite a display?

709
00:55:29,784 --> 00:55:30,910
What was?

710
00:55:30,994 --> 00:55:32,120
Everyone saw it.

711
00:55:32,787 --> 00:55:35,957
The Queen Mother talked about tarnishing
my reputation or whatever.

712
00:55:36,458 --> 00:55:38,126
And you taking my side.

713
00:55:40,962 --> 00:55:42,380
Wake up.

714
00:55:42,464 --> 00:55:44,299
Palace staff do not divulge
palace affairs.

715
00:55:47,427 --> 00:55:48,970
Do you really believe that?

716
00:55:50,638 --> 00:55:53,975
They say the mouth is
the gateway to disaster,

717
00:55:54,059 --> 00:55:56,853
and the tongue is
a blade that cuts the body.

718
00:55:57,354 --> 00:55:59,606
Do you know how many mouths were there?

719
00:56:02,442 --> 00:56:07,238
And you think not a single mouth there
has loose lips?

720
00:56:10,408 --> 00:56:14,496
They probably whipped up
an entire soap opera out of it by now.

721
00:56:17,499 --> 00:56:18,833
I can't believe it.

722
00:56:18,917 --> 00:56:20,835
And still in his ceremonial robe?

723
00:56:21,503 --> 00:56:22,712
I mean, it makes sense.

724
00:56:22,796 --> 00:56:24,756
I heard from an attendant
of the Queen Mother…

725
00:56:24,839 --> 00:56:26,674
I thought it was just a passing scandal,

726
00:56:26,758 --> 00:56:29,594
but as soon as she fainted,
he swept her up in his arms.

727
00:56:29,677 --> 00:56:30,887
It caused quite a stir.

728
00:56:30,970 --> 00:56:32,680
It must be true love!

729
00:56:32,764 --> 00:56:34,015
I know, right?

730
00:56:35,433 --> 00:56:37,143
Plenty of people weren't there.

731
00:56:37,227 --> 00:56:39,187
That doesn't make someone a suspect.

732
00:56:39,270 --> 00:56:41,231
She must've been
so shocked that she fainted.

733
00:56:44,317 --> 00:56:46,653
Your Majesty, are you all right?

734
00:56:46,736 --> 00:56:49,155
Please stay there. I will clean this up.

735
00:56:49,239 --> 00:56:50,323
Court Lady Im.

736
00:56:50,407 --> 00:56:51,616
Is anyone out there?

737
00:56:51,699 --> 00:56:52,909
Court Lady Im!

738
00:56:57,038 --> 00:56:58,832
What are your thoughts?

739
00:56:59,624 --> 00:57:00,667
Pardon?

740
00:57:00,750 --> 00:57:02,001
About what, Your Majesty?

741
00:57:03,378 --> 00:57:05,463
The Grand Prince and that maiden.

742
00:57:05,547 --> 00:57:07,257
Did they seem

743
00:57:08,591 --> 00:57:10,093
genuine in your eyes as well?

744
00:57:20,186 --> 00:57:22,230
- You're not coming with me?
- I have to work.

745
00:57:22,313 --> 00:57:23,523
But it's the weekend.

746
00:57:24,065 --> 00:57:25,066
If I clock out,

747
00:57:26,192 --> 00:57:27,318
someone will kill me.

748
00:57:27,402 --> 00:57:28,736
Who?

749
00:57:30,613 --> 00:57:31,990
Him.

750
00:57:33,199 --> 00:57:35,326
Oh.

751
00:57:36,327 --> 00:57:38,079
Try not to stay up too late, though.

752
00:57:38,663 --> 00:57:39,747
I shall try.

753
00:57:39,831 --> 00:57:41,916
You can call me
if you have trouble sleeping.

754
00:57:42,000 --> 00:57:43,376
I shall.

755
00:57:54,721 --> 00:57:56,306
The more mouths, the better, right?

756
00:58:47,065 --> 00:58:48,066
Your Ladyship!

757
00:58:51,945 --> 00:58:53,530
Are you all right?

758
00:58:53,613 --> 00:58:55,782
What about His Royal Highness?
Is he all right?

759
00:58:57,075 --> 00:58:58,076
Well…

760
00:59:00,203 --> 00:59:02,163
Our dear Steward Kim played a huge role.

761
00:59:02,247 --> 00:59:04,541
I am quite a biker, you see.

762
00:59:04,624 --> 00:59:06,125
Thank you.

763
00:59:07,377 --> 00:59:08,419
Ha!

764
00:59:08,503 --> 00:59:09,587
Applause please.

765
00:59:12,423 --> 00:59:14,092
Well done!

766
00:59:14,175 --> 00:59:15,176
<i>All right!</i>

767
00:59:15,260 --> 00:59:16,302
I'm exhausted.

768
00:59:39,826 --> 00:59:41,035
Still alive?

769
00:59:41,661 --> 00:59:43,580
<i>For now.</i>

770
00:59:45,039 --> 00:59:47,458
I haven't been able to eat,
so I'm starving.

771
00:59:47,542 --> 00:59:50,003
Why not? Is the food not to your liking?

772
00:59:50,086 --> 00:59:51,629
<i>No, I'm just trying to lose weight.</i>

773
00:59:52,130 --> 00:59:53,256
Why?

774
00:59:53,339 --> 00:59:55,341
Looking gaunt will make me
seem more like a victim.

775
00:59:58,177 --> 01:00:00,263
You'll have the Royal Guard
starting tomorrow.

776
01:00:00,888 --> 01:00:01,889
Really?

777
01:00:02,390 --> 01:00:04,309
Is that allowed
when we're not married yet?

778
01:00:04,392 --> 01:00:05,602
It isn't.

779
01:00:05,685 --> 01:00:06,728
I see.

780
01:00:07,228 --> 01:00:09,856
"Another crazy stunt pulled
by the infatuated Grand Prince"?

781
01:00:10,690 --> 01:00:12,567
I guess you can put it like that.

782
01:00:17,113 --> 01:00:18,489
Should I pull one too?

783
01:01:34,148 --> 01:01:36,317
Never thought I'd be doing this.

784
01:01:50,957 --> 01:01:54,794
This is the least we can do
to make them think we're madly in love.

785
01:01:56,212 --> 01:01:57,255
Oh, right.

786
01:02:01,843 --> 01:02:02,844
Here.

787
01:02:04,137 --> 01:02:06,639
This is the tea I drink
when I have trouble sleeping.

788
01:02:07,265 --> 01:02:09,225
It's really expensive, so don't waste it.

789
01:02:10,935 --> 01:02:12,895
One more thing…

790
01:02:15,273 --> 01:02:18,359
This is the magnesium supplement
I take when I really can't asleep.

791
01:02:19,235 --> 01:02:22,864
The side effect is nightmares,
but it's better than not sleeping at all.

792
01:02:25,950 --> 01:02:27,827
- When did I ever ask...
- Stop that.

793
01:02:28,745 --> 01:02:31,164
You didn't see a doctor
after what happened, did you?

794
01:02:35,752 --> 01:02:38,713
Don't you think I'd be
quite the supportive wife?

795
01:03:03,070 --> 01:03:04,155
What are you doing?

796
01:03:12,747 --> 01:03:13,748
Stay still.

797
01:03:53,162 --> 01:03:56,082
PERFECT CROWN

798
01:04:32,159 --> 01:04:33,953
<i>Why would I blush</i>

799
01:04:34,036 --> 01:04:36,873
and get all fluttery over a measly kiss?

800
01:04:36,956 --> 01:04:39,208
<i>You should have maintained decorum.</i>

801
01:04:39,292 --> 01:04:41,794
<i>Then what? Should we make it
a shotgun wedding?</i>

802
01:04:43,004 --> 01:04:45,882
Can I take you somewhere?
Let's speed things up a bit.

803
01:04:46,465 --> 01:04:49,093
<i>The quicker we get married,
the quicker we get divorced.</i>

804
01:04:50,052 --> 01:04:51,053
{\an8}Smile!

805
01:04:51,137 --> 01:04:53,890
{\an8}<i>Do you have that much time
to waste? I don't.</i>

806
01:04:54,515 --> 01:04:57,310
{\an8}<i>That maiden
should move out of your private residence.</i>

807
01:04:57,393 --> 01:05:00,229
{\an8}Do you have a plan?

808
01:05:01,022 --> 01:05:02,315
{\an8}Seong Huiju, what's wrong?

809
01:05:02,398 --> 01:05:05,192
{\an8}Jeongwoo! The brakes aren't working!

810
01:05:11,032 --> 01:05:13,326
{\an8}Why aren't you answering?

811
01:05:13,993 --> 01:05:16,287
{\an8}Will you take their side and not mine

812
01:05:16,370 --> 01:05:18,331
{\an8}because they're your family?

813
01:05:23,252 --> 01:05:24,420
{\an8}I will take your side.

814
01:05:33,262 --> 01:05:34,347
{\an8}I must appear

815
01:05:35,306 --> 01:05:36,849
{\an8}insanely infatuated with you…

816
01:05:45,858 --> 01:05:47,234
{\an8}…for people to believe

817
01:05:49,153 --> 01:05:50,738
{\an8}this absurd marriage is genuine.

818
01:06:07,838 --> 01:06:09,840
{\an8}- What's that?
- It's my <i>hopae</i>.

819
01:06:10,841 --> 01:06:11,842
{\an8}What about it?

820
01:06:13,260 --> 01:06:15,304
{\an8}Use it when you need a title behind you

821
01:06:15,388 --> 01:06:16,514
{\an8}or when you are afraid.

822
01:06:18,849 --> 01:06:21,811
{\an8}Does it summon a dragon
if I swing it around or something?

823
01:06:29,777 --> 01:06:30,778
{\an8}It'll summon me.

824
01:06:42,039 --> 01:06:44,041
{\an8}Translated by Justin S. Kim

825
01:06:55,344 --> 01:06:59,056
PERFECT CROWN
